  "notes": [
    "Initial data, full updates, partial rectangles and empty updates pass on ordinary, legacy shared and NT keyed textures. Input rows are padded and caller storage is overwritten immediately after each API call. Every readback checks all pixels, including unchanged pixels outside the rectangle.",
    "Shared uploads use an independent CPU-visible VidMm allocation and kernel-submitted copies. A partial update first reads the previous shared surface. A blocking write lock waits for the final submitted reader before releasing temporary storage. All upload and copy traffic is counted explicitly.",
    "The upload case performs 24 readbacks, uploads 119496 image bytes and copies 819200 allocation bytes, including padding, in staging operations. Its 32 submitted copies run on the kernel CPU worker. These are functional tests, not performance measurements.",
    "All five v29 sharing tests were rerun with the same new UMD and probe, including separate-process legacy and NT keyed ownership. Every process reports zero live allocations, live contexts, cleanup errors and rejected callbacks.",
    "No NPU execution, shaders, desktop rendering, cross-adapter output, presentation or Tahoma benchmark was performed. The physical host driver was not replaced."
